e('Aborting one is almost always better,','Aborting one can discard less work,','Unsupported frequency removed.')
e('A database\'s write-ahead log and undo records give it exactly this, so "abort the transaction" really means "preempt all its locks and roll back its changes".','Database recovery mechanisms can undo or invalidate a victim\'s transactional changes before releasing its transaction-scoped locks. The details differ: PostgreSQL uses MVCC tuple visibility rather than a general InnoDB-style undo log, and session-scoped locks need not be released by transaction rollback.','Do not equate WAL with generic undo or unlock before safe rollback.',pg+my)
